Object.assign(GT_BOOKS.fr.lines, {
  "Through the doors, a throne of black ink. The air goes perfectly still. Not a sound. Not even your own steps.": "Derrière les portes, un trône d'encre noire. L'air devient parfaitement immobile. Pas un bruit. Pas même tes propres pas.",
  "A tall figure in a robe of blank pages rises from it. Where his words should be, there is only ink.": "Une grande silhouette en robe de pages blanches s'en lève. Là où devraient être ses mots, il n'y a que de l'encre.",
  "{p}: You found my keys. You solved my riddles. How tiresome.": "{p} : Tu as trouvé mes clés. Tu as résolu mes énigmes. Quel ennui.",
  "{p}: Words. Noisy, messy, endless words. I will unwrite you first.": "{p} : Les mots. Bruyants, désordonnés, sans fin. Je vais d'abord te désécrire.",
  "💎 The {p}’s voice bursts out of the Unwriter’s throne, and the shards begin to sing.": "💎 La voix du {p} jaillit du trône du Désécriveur, et les éclats se mettent à chanter.",
  "At the top of the tower, a knight in black armor stands perfectly still.": "Au sommet de la tour, un chevalier en armure noire se tient parfaitement immobile.",
  "He has no mouth. When he speaks, the words appear in the air like smoke.": "Il n'a pas de bouche. Quand il parle, les mots apparaissent dans l'air comme de la fumée.",
  "{p}: My master is not here. But his shards are. And I will keep them.": "{p} : Mon maître n'est pas ici. Mais ses éclats, si. Et je vais les garder.",
  "The Herald’s armor falls apart, empty. A last smoky word drifts away: “castle”.": "L'armure du Héraut s'effondre, vide. Un dernier mot de fumée s'envole : « château ».",
  "Behind him, the shards of the {p} glow on a stone table.": "Derrière lui, les éclats du {p} brillent sur une table de pierre.",
  "💎 You found the <b>last {p} Shards</b>! Every shard is together at last, but they are silent.": "💎 Tu as trouvé les <b>derniers éclats du {p}</b> ! Ils sont enfin tous réunis, mais ils restent muets.",
  "{p} has hidden away the {p}’s voice.": "{p} a caché la voix du {p}.",
  "Take the shards home to {p} in {p}, {p}.": "Rapporte les éclats à {p} à {p}, {p}.",
  "{p}: {p}… all the shards. I never dreamed I would see the whole {p} again.": "{p} : {p}… tous les éclats. Je n'aurais jamais cru revoir le {p} entier.",
  "But listen: it does not sing. {p} has locked its voice away in <b>Castle Unwritten</b>, in the {p} far to the north-east.": "Mais écoute : il ne chante pas. {p} a enfermé sa voix au <b>Château Non-Écrit</b>, dans les {p}, loin au nord-est.",
  "The castle gate opens only for three keys, hidden long ago at the edges of the world:": "La porte du château ne s'ouvre qu'avec trois clés, cachées il y a longtemps aux confins du monde :",
  "🪶 the <b>Dawn Quill</b>, high in the {p} in the north,": "🪶 la <b>Plume de l'Aube</b>, haut dans les {p}, au nord,",
  "🫙 the <b>Dusk Inkwell</b>, lost in the {p} in the south,": "🫙 l'<b>Encrier du Crépuscule</b>, perdu dans les {p}, au sud,",
  "⭐ and the <b>Star Seal</b>, fallen into the {p} in the far south.": "⭐ et le <b>Sceau Étoilé</b>, tombé dans le {p}, tout au sud.",
  "I have ordered the old roads opened: north and south of Aldermere, north and south of Seravel. Your ship can sail north and south from the Eastern Isles too.": "J'ai fait rouvrir les vieilles routes : au nord et au sud d'Aldermere, au nord et au sud de Seravel. Ton navire peut aussi naviguer au nord et au sud depuis les Îles de l'Est.",
  "Ask in the taverns. People remember more than they think. Go, and bring back our words!": "Renseigne-toi dans les tavernes. Les gens se souviennent de plus de choses qu'ils ne le pensent. Va, et rapporte-nous nos mots !",
  "{p}: All three keys! Castle Unwritten is in the {p}, far to the north-east. End this, hero.": "{p} : Les trois clés ! Le Château Non-Écrit est dans les {p}, loin au nord-est. Mets fin à tout ça, héros.",
  "✨ Something glints between the rocks… you dig it out.": "✨ Quelque chose brille entre les rochers… tu le dégages.",
  "🪶 You found the <b>Dawn Quill</b>! A golden quill that writes light. (Key {n} of {n})": "🪶 Tu as trouvé la <b>Plume de l'Aube</b> ! Une plume dorée qui écrit la lumière. (Clé {n} sur {n})",
  "✨ Deep in the trees, a little pool of shadow… no, an inkwell, sitting on a mossy stone.": "✨ Au fond des arbres, une petite flaque d'ombre… non, un encrier, posé sur une pierre moussue.",
  "🫙 You found the <b>Dusk Inkwell</b>! Its ink is the color of the evening sky. (Key {n} of {n})": "🫙 Tu as trouvé l'<b>Encrier du Crépuscule</b> ! Son encre a la couleur du ciel du soir. (Clé {n} sur {n})",
  "✨ Something in the dust of the gully twinkles like a fallen star.": "✨ Quelque chose dans la poussière du ravin scintille comme une étoile tombée.",
  "⭐ You found the <b>Star Seal</b>! A silver seal shaped like a star. (Key {n} of {n})": "⭐ Tu as trouvé le <b>Sceau Étoilé</b> ! Un sceau d'argent en forme d'étoile. (Clé {n} sur {n})",
  "🔑 The quill, the inkwell and the star hum together in your bag.": "🔑 La plume, l'encrier et l'étoile vibrent ensemble dans ton sac.",
  "Castle Unwritten’s gate will open for you now. It stands in the {p}, in the far north-east.": "La porte du Château Non-Écrit s'ouvrira pour toi maintenant. Il se dresse dans les {p}, tout au nord-est.",
  "The cave floor is a frozen lake. Under the ice, two cold eyes open.": "Le sol de la grotte est un lac gelé. Sous la glace, deux yeux froids s'ouvrent.",
  "A wyrm of ice smashes up through the floor!": "Un dragon de glace jaillit à travers le sol !",
  "{p} shatters into a thousand glittering pieces.": "{p} se brise en mille éclats scintillants.",
  "Wind howls up the shaft. A giant bird made of storm clouds lands in front of you.": "Le vent hurle dans le puits. Un oiseau géant fait de nuages d'orage se pose devant toi.",
  "{p}: SKREEEEE!": "{p} : SKRIIIIII !",
  "{p} dissolves into a harmless spring rain.": "{p} se dissout en une petite pluie de printemps inoffensive.",
  "A skeleton in a scholar’s robe looks up from a book of black pages.": "Un squelette en robe de savant lève les yeux d'un livre aux pages noires.",
  "{p}: Ah, visitors. Let me write you… an ending.": "{p} : Ah, des visiteurs. Laissez-moi vous écrire… une fin.",
  "{p}’s book slams shut, and he crumbles to dust with it.": "Le livre de {p} se referme d'un coup, et il tombe en poussière avec lui.",
  "The temple floor cracks. Vines as thick as trees rise up, each with a snapping head.": "Le sol du temple se fend. Des lianes épaisses comme des arbres se dressent, chacune avec une tête qui mord.",
  "{p} hisses from three mouths at once!": "{p} siffle par trois bouches à la fois !",
  "{p} withers and sinks back into the ground.": "{p} se fane et s'enfonce dans le sol.",
  "The water in the barrow bubbles. A huge shape of mud and weeds rises, wearing a crown of reeds.": "L'eau du tertre bouillonne. Une énorme forme de boue et d'algues se dresse, coiffée d'une couronne de roseaux.",
  "{p}: You are tracking mud into my palace!": "{p} : Tu mets de la boue partout dans mon palais !",
  "{p} slumps back into a harmless puddle. Her crown floats away.": "{p} s'effondre en une flaque inoffensive. Sa couronne s'en va en flottant.",
  "Hot wind fills the cave. A red wyvern drops from the ceiling, wings spread wide.": "Un vent chaud remplit la grotte. Une vouivre rouge tombe du plafond, les ailes déployées.",
  "{p} roars, and the whole canyon roars with it!": "{p} rugit, et tout le canyon rugit avec elle !",
  "{p} flees out of a crack in the rock, never to return.": "{p} s'enfuit par une fente dans la roche et ne revient jamais.",
  "💰 {p} guarded a pile of treasure!": "💰 {p} gardait un tas de trésors !",
  "💰 {p}’s nest is full of shiny things!": "💰 Le nid du {p} est plein de choses brillantes !",
  "💰 {p}’s hoard is yours!": "💰 Le trésor du {p} est à toi !",
  "💰 Treasure hidden among the roots!": "💰 Un trésor caché entre les racines !",
  "💰 {p}’s treasure, a little muddy.": "💰 Le trésor de {p}, un peu boueux.",
  "💰 The wyvern’s hoard glitters in the dark!": "💰 Le trésor de la vouivre scintille dans le noir !",
  "The three keys rise out of your bag and fit into the sockets.": "Les trois clés sortent de ton sac et se glissent dans les encoches.",
  "With a sound like a book opening, Castle Unwritten’s gate swings wide.": "Avec un bruit de livre qui s'ouvre, la porte du Château Non-Écrit s'ouvre en grand.",
  "You pull the {p} lever. Its flame goes out.": "Tu abaisses le levier {p}. Sa flamme s'éteint.",
  "🔥 Sun, star… and the moon asleep. The iron gate grinds upward!": "🔥 Soleil, étoile… et la lune endormie. La grille de fer remonte en grinçant !",
  "✨ The plate glows.": "✨ La dalle brille.",
  "The plates sink back into the floor with a groan.": "Les dalles retombent dans le sol avec un grondement.",
  "Read the poem again: in what order does the night pass?": "Relis le poème : dans quel ordre passe la nuit ?",
  "🔥 All four plates blaze with light. The iron gate grinds upward!": "🔥 Les quatre dalles flamboient de lumière. La grille de fer remonte en grinçant !",
  "🗿 {p}: “Answer my word, traveler.”": "🗿 {p} : « Réponds à mon mot, voyageur. »",
  "🗿 {p}: “True words.” Its eyes glow gold.": "🗿 {p} : « Des mots vrais. » Ses yeux brillent d'or.",
  "🗿 {p}: “Not true. Come back when you know.”": "🗿 {p} : « Ce n'est pas vrai. Reviens quand tu sauras. »",
  "🗿 All three statues glow. The great doors to the throne room swing open!": "🗿 Les trois statues brillent. Les grandes portes de la salle du trône s'ouvrent !",
  "Welcome to {p}. The King awaits brave souls.": "Bienvenue au {p}. Le Roi attend des âmes courageuses.",
  "{p}’s last guards block the stairs!": "Les derniers gardes de {p} bloquent l'escalier !",
  "Keep warm! The {p} Wolves hunt in packs out on the tundra.": "Couvre-toi bien ! Les loups de {p} chassent en meute dans la toundra.",
  "East of here the land turns to rock and thunder: the {p}.": "À l'est, la terre devient roche et tonnerre : les {p}.",
  "I built a snow knight yesterday. It has a sword made of an icicle!": "Hier, j'ai fait un chevalier de neige. Il a une épée en glaçon !",
  "Thunder Hawks steal our hats. Every. Single. Day.": "Les faucons du tonnerre nous volent nos chapeaux. Tous. Les. Jours.",
  "Further east the land goes black. Nothing grows in the {p}.": "Plus à l'est, la terre devient noire. Rien ne pousse dans les {p}.",
  "The mine’s gold paid for this town. Now monsters dig there instead.": "L'or de la mine a payé ce village. Maintenant, ce sont les monstres qui creusent.",
  "We are the last town before the castle. Buy {p}: the wraiths out there love curses.": "Nous sommes le dernier village avant le château. Achète de l'{p} : les spectres là-bas adorent les malédictions.",
  "The Blighted Crypt is north-west of here. A Lich Scribe writes death verses down there.": "La Crypte Flétrie est au nord-ouest d'ici. Un Scribe Liche y écrit des vers de mort.",
  "Mum says not to look at the castle at night. I looked. It looked back.": "Maman dit de ne pas regarder le château la nuit. Je l'ai regardé. Il m'a regardé aussi.",
  "Vine Serpents bite. Carry Antidotes, always.": "Les serpents-lianes mordent. Emporte toujours des antidotes.",
  "North is Aldermere. East is the {p}. Mind your boots.": "Au nord, c'est Aldermere. À l'est, le {p}. Attention à tes bottes.",
  "A parrot taught me a rude word. I won’t say it.": "Un perroquet m'a appris un gros mot. Je ne le dirai pas.",
  "Rot Caps puff poison. Hold your breath. Or just bring Antidotes.": "Les champignons pourris crachent du poison. Retiens ton souffle. Ou emporte des antidotes.",
  "The road north goes back up to Seravel, through the canyon road.": "La route du nord remonte à Seravel par la route du canyon.",
  "I caught a frog the size of my head! Then it caught me.": "J'ai attrapé une grenouille grosse comme ma tête ! Puis c'est elle qui m'a attrapé.",
  "The sea north of here leads back to the Eastern Isles, if you have a boat.": "La mer au nord d'ici ramène aux Îles de l'Est, si tu as un bateau.",
  "Sun Scarabs flash so bright you can’t see. Squint!": "Les scarabées solaires brillent tellement qu'on n'y voit rien. Plisse les yeux !",
  "Yell in the canyon and it yells back. I yelled my name forty times.": "Crie dans le canyon et il te répond. J'ai crié mon nom quarante fois.",
  "The way ahead is guarded!": "Le chemin est gardé !",
  "The Hoarfrost Cavern is north-east of town. Something huge sleeps in the ice down there.": "La Caverne de Givre est au nord-est du village. Quelque chose d'énorme dort dans la glace, là-dessous.",
  "The old road south goes back to Aldermere. The King opened it for you, they say.": "La vieille route du sud ramène à Aldermere. On dit que le Roi l'a ouverte pour toi.",
  "Pray, rest, and be brave. {p} fears words spoken with courage.": "Prie, repose-toi et sois courageux. {p} craint les mots dits avec courage.",
  "The Dawn Quill? A shepherd swore she saw a golden glint on the peak above the old mine, in the north-west.": "La Plume de l'Aube ? Une bergère jure avoir vu un reflet doré sur le sommet au-dessus de la vieille mine, au nord-ouest.",
  "The Thunder Mine runs deep. A Storm Roc nests at the bottom.": "La Mine du Tonnerre est très profonde. Un Roc des Tempêtes niche tout au fond.",
  "Castle Unwritten is east of town. Its gate has three sockets: a quill, an inkwell and a star.": "Le Château Non-Écrit est à l'est du village. Sa porte a trois encoches : une plume, un encrier et une étoile.",
  "Inside the castle, the old guards say, the doors only open for the clever. Levers, plates and talking statues.": "Dans le château, disent les vieux gardes, les portes ne s'ouvrent qu'aux malins. Leviers, dalles et statues qui parlent.",
  "The Dusk Inkwell? Old Ma {p} talks about a grove nobody can find, deep in the trees in the south-east.": "L'Encrier du Crépuscule ? La vieille Ma {p} parle d'un bosquet que personne ne trouve, au fond des arbres, au sud-est.",
  "The Overgrown Temple is north-east. A Vine Hydra grew out of the floor in there!": "Le Temple Envahi est au nord-est. Une Hydre-Liane est sortie du sol là-dedans !",
  "The Drowned Barrow is south-west of town, past the reeds. {p} rules it.": "Le Tertre Noyé est au sud-ouest du village, après les roseaux. {p} y règne.",
  "The canyon east of here is dry as bone. Opposite of here, really.": "Le canyon à l'est d'ici est sec comme un os. Tout le contraire d'ici, en fait.",
  "The Star Seal? There’s a gully in the far west, past the red cliffs, where the stars fall at night.": "Le Sceau Étoilé ? Il y a un ravin tout à l'ouest, après les falaises rouges, où les étoiles tombent la nuit.",
  "The Echo Canyon Caves are south-east. A Canyon Wyvern roosts at the bottom.": "Les Grottes du Canyon de l'Écho sont au sud-est. Une Vouivre du Canyon perche tout au fond.",
  "🪨 Words are carved into the stone:": "🪨 Des mots sont gravés dans la pierre :",
  "“Wake the Sun and the Star, but let the Moon sleep.”": "« Réveille le Soleil et l'Étoile, mais laisse dormir la Lune. »",
  "“Beware: every lever stirs the one beside it.”": "« Attention : chaque levier fait bouger son voisin. »",
  "Two Ink Sentinels step out of the shadows!": "Deux sentinelles d'encre sortent de l'ombre !",
  "🪨 A poem is carved into the stone:": "🪨 Un poème est gravé dans la pierre :",
  "“First the quill writes the dawn, then the sun climbs high,”": "« D'abord la plume écrit l'aube, puis le soleil monte haut, »",
  "“the moon follows after, and a star closes the sky.”": "« la lune le suit, et une étoile ferme le ciel. »",
  "Four plates are set into the floor: 🪶 ☀️ 🌙 ⭐": "Quatre dalles sont posées dans le sol : 🪶 ☀️ 🌙 ⭐",
  "The Statue of Dawn": "La Statue de l'Aube",
  "The Statue of Noon": "La Statue de Midi",
  "The Statue of Dusk": "La Statue du Crépuscule",
  "🪨 “Speak true words to the three statues, and the last door will open.”": "🪨 « Dis des mots vrais aux trois statues, et la dernière porte s'ouvrira. »",
  "{p}: Rare goods from across the sea! Take a look.": "{p} : Des marchandises rares venues d'outre-mer ! Jette un œil.",
  "{p}: Blades and bows from faraway smithies!": "{p} : Des lames et des arcs de forges lointaines !",
  "Welcome to {p}, the west harbor of Aldermere! Ships come and go all day.": "Bienvenue à {p}, le port ouest d'Aldermere ! Les navires vont et viennent toute la journée.",
  "Sail north along the coast and you reach the {p}. South takes you to the jungle.": "Navigue vers le nord le long de la côte et tu atteins la {p}. Vers le sud, c'est la jungle.",
  "There’s a shrine on a little island just south of here. Sailors pray there before a long trip.": "Il y a un sanctuaire sur une petite île juste au sud d'ici. Les marins y prient avant un long voyage.",
  "{p} never freezes. The sea keeps moving, so the ice can’t catch it.": "{p} ne gèle jamais. La mer bouge sans arrêt, alors la glace ne l'attrape pas.",
  "East along the north coast is the Thundercrag shore, and past that, the black Inkblight sea.": "À l'est le long de la côte nord, il y a le rivage de Thundercrag, et plus loin, la mer noire d'Inkblight.",
  "An island shrine sits just off the coast, north of here. Ice all around it, but warm inside.": "Un sanctuaire se trouve sur une île juste au large, au nord d'ici. De la glace tout autour, mais il fait chaud dedans.",
  "{p}! Best fish on the whole continent. Don’t tell the Marsh folk I said that.": "{p} ! Le meilleur poisson du continent. Ne dis pas aux gens du marais que j'ai dit ça.",
  "You can sail up the river from here, right into the heart of the jungle.": "D'ici, tu peux remonter la rivière en bateau jusqu'au cœur de la jungle.",
  "East along the coast is {p}, then the red canyon. The whole south shore is one long sea road.": "À l'est le long de la côte, il y a {p}, puis le canyon rouge. Toute la côte sud est une longue route maritime.",
  "{p} sits where the marsh meets the sea. Mind the eels at low tide.": "{p} se trouve là où le marais rejoint la mer. Attention aux anguilles à marée basse.",
  "The sea lanes go all the way round the continent now that the King opened them.": "Les routes maritimes font le tour du continent maintenant que le Roi les a ouvertes.",
  "Old story: there’s a shrine out on the water, east of here, that heals even the fallen.": "Une vieille histoire : il y a un sanctuaire sur l'eau, à l'est d'ici, qui soigne même ceux qui sont tombés.",
  "Every coast of the continent is linked by sea now. Sail all the way round if you like!": "Toutes les côtes du continent sont reliées par la mer. Fais le tour complet si tu veux !",
  "Island shrines heal the whole crew. Steer close and pray from the deck.": "Les sanctuaires des îles soignent tout l'équipage. Approche-toi et prie depuis le pont.",
  "I pray here before every voyage. The sea is kinder to the faithful.": "Je prie ici avant chaque voyage. La mer est plus douce avec les fidèles.",
  "{p}: Welcome to our home, young hero. Do look around. The library is my favourite room.": "{p} : Bienvenue chez nous, jeune héros. Fais le tour. La bibliothèque est ma pièce préférée.",
  "{p}: The cook makes the best honey bread in the kingdom. Tell him I sent you.": "{p} : Le cuisinier fait le meilleur pain au miel du royaume. Dis-lui que je t'envoie.",
  "{p}: Stand tall before the King!": "{p} : Tiens-toi droit devant le Roi !",
  "{p}: Nobody gets near the thrones without our say-so.": "{p} : Personne n'approche des trônes sans notre permission.",
  "{p}: One day I’ll go on an adventure too! Father says I must learn my words first.": "{p} : Un jour, moi aussi je partirai à l'aventure ! Père dit que je dois d'abord apprendre mes mots.",
  "{p}: Did you know there are chests in three colors? Ruby, sapphire and emerald. Each needs its own key.": "{p} : Tu savais qu'il y a des coffres de trois couleurs ? Rubis, saphir et émeraude. Chacun a besoin de sa propre clé.",
  "{p}: Shh! This is the royal library. Every book here was written with the old {p}.": "{p} : Chut ! C'est la bibliothèque royale. Chaque livre ici a été écrit avec l'ancien {p}.",
  "{p}: Read a little every day and the words will stay with you.": "{p} : Lis un peu chaque jour et les mots resteront avec toi.",
  "{p}: I’m supposed to be dusting the shelves… but this book about sea monsters is really good.": "{p} : Je suis censé dépoussiérer les étagères… mais ce livre sur les monstres marins est vraiment bien.",
  "{p}: Mind the hot stove! Honey bread for the King, stew for the guards.": "{p} : Attention au fourneau ! Pain au miel pour le Roi, ragoût pour les gardes.",
  "{p}: Hungry? Inns are the place for a hot meal and a warm bed.": "{p} : Faim ? Les auberges, c'est l'endroit pour un repas chaud et un bon lit.",
  "{p}: Twelve loaves, six pies and a cake for the Prince. And the day has only started!": "{p} : Douze pains, six tartes et un gâteau pour le Prince. Et la journée ne fait que commencer !",
  "{p}: Night shift tonight. I’m resting my feet while I can.": "{p} : Je suis de garde cette nuit. Je repose mes pieds tant que je peux.",
  "{p}: My guards keep the towns safe. If you see a pickpocket, call for us!": "{p} : Mes gardes protègent les villages. Si tu vois un pickpocket, appelle-nous !",
  "{p}: Every town has a jail now. Thieves spend a night behind bars, or pay a fine.": "{p} : Chaque village a une prison maintenant. Les voleurs passent une nuit derrière les barreaux, ou paient une amende.",
  "{p}: Father keeps the Ruby Key in the treasury, downstairs on this side.": "{p} : Père garde la Clé de Rubis dans la salle du trésor, en bas, de ce côté.",
  "{p}: {p} of Seravel keeps the Sapphire Key. And the Emerald Key? Lost at sea, somewhere far to the south-east.": "{p} : {p} de Seravel garde la Clé de Saphir. Et la Clé d'Émeraude ? Perdue en mer, quelque part loin au sud-est.",
  "{p}: The Princess’s room must be spotless. She notices every speck of dust!": "{p} : La chambre de la Princesse doit être impeccable. Elle remarque le moindre grain de poussière !",
  "{p}: The royal dinner is at sundown. Forty guests, sixty candles.": "{p} : Le dîner royal est au coucher du soleil. Quarante invités, soixante bougies.",
  "{p}: Taxes, letters, maps… a chancellor’s work is never done.": "{p} : Impôts, lettres, cartes… le travail d'un chancelier n'est jamais fini.",
  "{p}: I came all the way from {p} for the feast. Isn’t the hall lovely?": "{p} : Je suis venue de {p} exprès pour le festin. La salle n'est-elle pas magnifique ?",
  "{p}: The King says you may open the treasury chests. The Ruby Key is in the locked one.": "{p} : Le Roi dit que tu peux ouvrir les coffres du trésor. La Clé de Rubis est dans celui qui est fermé à clé.",
  "{p}: Spell its word to open the lock. Then the key opens every ruby-red chest you find.": "{p} : Écris son mot pour ouvrir le cadenas. Ensuite, la clé ouvre tous les coffres rouge rubis que tu trouveras.",
  "{p}: Good day! The great hall gets so dusty with all these visitors.": "{p} : Bonjour ! La grande salle prend tellement la poussière avec tous ces visiteurs.",
  "{p}: Welcome to {p}. The King is at the far end of the hall.": "{p} : Bienvenue au {p}. Le Roi est au fond de la salle.",
  "{p}: The town is just outside. Enjoy your visit!": "{p} : Le village est juste dehors. Bonne visite !",
  "{p}: My mother rules Seravel from this throne. I’m learning to sail, so I can visit every coast!": "{p} : Ma mère règne sur Seravel depuis ce trône. J'apprends à naviguer pour visiter toutes les côtes !",
  "{p}: The Sapphire Key? It’s in our treasury, of course. Ask the guard there.": "{p} : La Clé de Saphir ? Elle est dans notre salle du trésor, bien sûr. Demande au garde.",
  "{p}: Bow to Her Majesty, {p}!": "{p} : Inclinez-vous devant Sa Majesté, {p} !",
  "{p}: The sun never sets on Seravel. Well… it does. But slowly.": "{p} : Le soleil ne se couche jamais sur Seravel. Enfin… si. Mais lentement.",
  "{p}: These shelves hold maps of every coast and island. The seas link all the way round now!": "{p} : Ces étagères gardent les cartes de toutes les côtes et îles. Les mers font le tour complet maintenant !",
  "{p}: Old charts say the Emerald Key sank with a ship near an island in the south-east.": "{p} : Les vieilles cartes disent que la Clé d'Émeraude a coulé avec un navire près d'une île du sud-est.",
  "{p}: I am copying a map of the Sunken Archive. One wrong line and someone gets lost!": "{p} : Je recopie une carte des Archives Englouties. Une ligne de travers et quelqu'un se perd !",
  "{p}: Spiced rice, date cakes and mint tea. Palace food is the best in the desert!": "{p} : Riz épicé, gâteaux aux dattes et thé à la menthe. La cuisine du palais est la meilleure du désert !",
  "{p}: Try not to steal from the townsfolk. The jail food is terrible, I hear.": "{p} : Évite de voler les gens du village. Il paraît que la nourriture de la prison est affreuse.",
  "{p}: Fresh oranges from the oasis! The Queen loves them.": "{p} : Des oranges fraîches de l'oasis ! La Reine les adore.",
  "{p}: Sand in my boots again. Sand everywhere!": "{p} : Encore du sable dans mes bottes. Du sable partout !",
  "{p}: My guards watch the market. Pickpockets end up in the town jail.": "{p} : Mes gardes surveillent le marché. Les pickpockets finissent en prison.",
  "{p}: Pay the fine, or work it off with honest words. Your choice.": "{p} : Paie l'amende, ou rembourse-la avec des mots honnêtes. À toi de choisir.",
  "{p}: A ruby chest, a sapphire chest, an emerald chest… a key for each color. Once you have a key, it’s yours for good.": "{p} : Un coffre rubis, un coffre saphir, un coffre émeraude… une clé pour chaque couleur. Une fois que tu as une clé, elle est à toi pour toujours.",
  "{p}: I saw a blue sapphire chest in the desert once. Maybe you’ll find it!": "{p} : Un jour, j'ai vu un coffre bleu saphir dans le désert. Tu le trouveras peut-être !",
  "{p}: The Princess wants her blue silk ready for the feast.": "{p} : La Princesse veut sa soie bleue prête pour le festin.",
  "{p}: The dining hall is ready for the ambassadors from Aldermere.": "{p} : La salle à manger est prête pour les ambassadeurs d'Aldermere.",
  "{p}: Every ship that sails the Royal dock brings news from across the sea.": "{p} : Chaque navire qui part du quai royal apporte des nouvelles d'outre-mer.",
  "{p}: I bring greetings from {p}. What a beautiful palace!": "{p} : J'apporte les salutations de {p}. Quel beau palais !",
  "{p}: The Queen allows you into the treasury. The Sapphire Key is in the word-locked chest.": "{p} : La Reine te permet d'entrer dans la salle du trésor. La Clé de Saphir est dans le coffre au cadenas à mots.",
  "{p}: Spell its word, and every sapphire-blue chest in the world will open for you.": "{p} : Écris son mot, et tous les coffres bleu saphir du monde s'ouvriront pour toi.",
  "{p}: Mind the carpet, it’s freshly brushed!": "{p} : Attention au tapis, il vient d'être brossé !",
  "{p}: Welcome to {p}. Her Majesty is at the end of the hall.": "{p} : Bienvenue au {p}. Sa Majesté est au fond de la salle.",
  "{p}: {p} is right outside. Ships leave from the Royal dock.": "{p} : {p} est juste dehors. Les navires partent du quai royal.",
  "{p}: I only borrowed a loaf of bread! Honest!": "{p} : J'ai juste emprunté un pain ! Promis !",
  "{p}: Forty years I picked pockets. Then I picked the Captain’s. Big mistake.": "{p} : Quarante ans que je vole des portefeuilles. Puis j'ai volé celui du Capitaine. Grosse erreur.",
  "{p}: Keep your hands in your own pockets and you’ll never see the inside of a cell.": "{p} : Garde tes mains dans tes poches et tu ne verras jamais l'intérieur d'une cellule.",
  "The roads north and south of the old kingdoms are open again. Strange lands out there!": "Les routes au nord et au sud des vieux royaumes sont de nouveau ouvertes. Des terres étranges là-bas !",
  "Some treasures are hidden in plain sight. Walk where nobody walks.": "Certains trésors sont cachés à la vue de tous. Marche là où personne ne marche.",
  "The whole continent is ringed by sea. With a ship you can reach every coast.": "Tout le continent est entouré par la mer. Avec un navire, tu peux atteindre toutes les côtes.",
  "Island shrines! Sail up close and pray from your boat.": "Des sanctuaires sur les îles ! Approche-toi en bateau et prie depuis le pont.",
  "Watch your purse in the market! There are pickpockets about.": "Attention à ta bourse au marché ! Il y a des pickpockets.",
  "Every town has a jail now. Thieves get a night behind bars.": "Chaque village a une prison maintenant. Les voleurs passent une nuit derrière les barreaux.",
  "Have you seen the colored chests? Ruby, sapphire, emerald… each wants its own key.": "Tu as vu les coffres de couleur ? Rubis, saphir, émeraude… chacun veut sa propre clé.",
  "A smooth, frosted pebble of glass. Worth {n} gold at any shop.": "Un galet de verre lisse et dépoli. Vaut {n} pièces d'or dans n'importe quelle boutique.",
  "Hold it to your ear and hear the sea. Worth {n} gold.": "Mets-le contre ton oreille et entends la mer. Vaut {n} pièces d'or.",
  "A sailor’s ring, a little tarnished. Worth {n} gold.": "Une bague de marin, un peu ternie. Vaut {n} pièces d'or.",
  "A perfect round pearl. Worth {n} gold.": "Une perle parfaitement ronde. Vaut {n} pièces d'or.",
  "A tiny statue carved from red coral. Worth {n} gold.": "Une petite statue sculptée dans du corail rouge. Vaut {n} pièces d'or.",
  "A pouch of old pirate coins. Worth {n} gold.": "Une bourse de vieilles pièces de pirates. Vaut {n} pièces d'or.",
  "A crown from a kingdom lost to the sea. Worth {n} gold.": "Une couronne d'un royaume englouti par la mer. Vaut {n} pièces d'or.",
  "A deep blue gem with a star inside. Worth {n} gold.": "Une gemme bleu profond avec une étoile à l'intérieur. Vaut {n} pièces d'or.",
  "Snow and fallen rock block the way.": "La neige et des rochers tombés bloquent le passage.",
  "{p} may know how to open the old roads north and south.": "{p} sait peut-être comment ouvrir les vieilles routes du nord et du sud.",
  "Thick black fog hangs over the sea to the north.": "Un épais brouillard noir recouvre la mer au nord.",
  "{p} may know what lies beyond it.": "{p} sait peut-être ce qu'il y a au-delà.",
  "A wall of storms blocks the southern sea.": "Un mur de tempêtes bloque la mer du sud.",
  "Black gates as tall as trees. Three empty sockets glow faintly in the stone:": "Des portes noires hautes comme des arbres. Trois encoches vides brillent faiblement dans la pierre :",
  "a quill, an inkwell and a star. Without all three keys, the castle will not open.": "une plume, un encrier et une étoile. Sans les trois clés, le château ne s'ouvrira pas.",
  "Storms block the open sea.": "Des tempêtes bloquent la haute mer.",
  "{p} may know when the old sea lanes open.": "{p} sait peut-être quand les vieilles routes maritimes s'ouvriront.",
  "You found something!": "Tu as trouvé quelque chose !",
  "🔑 You got the <b>{p}</b>! 🔴": "🔑 Tu as reçu la <b>{p}</b> ! 🔴",
  "🔑 You got the <b>{p}</b>! 🔵": "🔑 Tu as reçu la <b>{p}</b> ! 🔵",
  "🔑 You got the <b>{p}</b>! 🟢": "🔑 Tu as reçu la <b>{p}</b> ! 🟢",
  "It opens every ruby chest in the world, and it stays with you for good.": "Elle ouvre tous les coffres rubis du monde, et elle reste avec toi pour toujours.",
  "It opens every sapphire chest in the world, and it stays with you for good.": "Elle ouvre tous les coffres saphir du monde, et elle reste avec toi pour toujours.",
  "It opens every emerald chest in the world, and it stays with you for good.": "Elle ouvre tous les coffres émeraude du monde, et elle reste avec toi pour toujours.",
  "🔴 A ruby chest! Its keyhole is shaped like a ruby.": "🔴 Un coffre rubis ! Sa serrure a la forme d'un rubis.",
  "🔵 A sapphire chest! Its keyhole is shaped like a sapphire.": "🔵 Un coffre saphir ! Sa serrure a la forme d'un saphir.",
  "🟢 A emerald chest! Its keyhole is shaped like a emerald.": "🟢 Un coffre émeraude ! Sa serrure a la forme d'une émeraude.",
  "It only opens with the <b>{p}</b>.": "Il ne s'ouvre qu'avec la <b>{p}</b>.",
  "The {p} is kept in the treasury of {p}.": "La {p} est gardée dans la salle du trésor du {p}.",
  "The {p} is kept in the treasury of {p}, in {p}.": "La {p} est gardée dans la salle du trésor du {p}, à {p}.",
  "Old charts say the {p} lies on a far island in the south-east sea.": "Les vieilles cartes disent que la {p} se trouve sur une île lointaine de la mer du sud-est.",
  "🔑 The {p} turns with a click… 🔴": "🔑 La {p} tourne avec un déclic… 🔴",
  "🔑 The {p} turns with a click… 🔵": "🔑 La {p} tourne avec un déclic… 🔵",
  "🔑 The {p} turns with a click… 🟢": "🔑 La {p} tourne avec un déclic… 🟢",
  "🚨 A guard makes you pay {n} gold back. Behave yourself!": "🚨 Un garde te fait rendre {n} pièces d'or. Tiens-toi bien !",
  "🔒 Clang! The cell door slams shut behind you.": "🔒 Clang ! La porte de la cellule claque derrière toi.",
  "Talk to the {p} through the bars to get out.": "Parle au {p} à travers les barreaux pour sortir.",
  "You pay {n} gold.": "Tu paies {n} pièces d'or.",
  "🔓 Clank! The cell door swings open.": "🔓 Clac ! La porte de la cellule s'ouvre.",
  "{p}: Off you go. And stay out of other folks’ pockets!": "{p} : Tu peux partir. Et ne mets plus la main dans les poches des autres !",
  "{p}: Visiting? Keep your hands in your own pockets and you’ll never stay here.": "{p} : En visite ? Garde tes mains dans tes poches et tu ne resteras jamais ici.",
  "👮 {p}: “Caught with your hand in a pocket, eh?” · 💰 {n}": "👮 {p} : « Pris la main dans une poche, hein ? » · 💰 {n}",
  "💰 Pay the fine ({n} gold)": "💰 Payer l'amende ({n} pièces d'or)",
  "🧽 Scrub the floors (answer {n} words right)": "🧽 Frotter le sol (réponds juste à {n} mots)",
  "Honest work, honest words.": "Travail honnête, mots honnêtes.",
  "⏳ Wait": "⏳ Attendre",
  "You sit on the cold stone floor. Nobody comes to let you out.": "Tu t'assois sur le sol de pierre froid. Personne ne vient te libérer.",
  "✨ The floors are sparkling!": "✨ Le sol brille !",
  "{p}: Not bad. Not bad at all.": "{p} : Pas mal. Pas mal du tout.",
  "🧽 Scrubbing the floor… {n}/{n}": "🧽 Tu frottes le sol… {n}/{n}",
  "{p}: Missed a spot! Keep going.": "{p} : Tu as oublié une tache ! Continue.",
  "💬 Talk": "💬 Parler",
  "🤏 Pick their pocket": "🤏 Faire les poches",
  "They’re watching you now.": "Il te surveille maintenant.",
  "Their pockets are empty now.": "Ses poches sont vides maintenant.",
  "A guard is watching! Move away first.": "Un garde regarde ! Éloigne-toi d'abord.",
  "Listen for the word and pick it. Wrong means jail!": "Écoute le mot et choisis-le. Si tu te trompes, c'est la prison !",
  "🤏 Sneaky… which word do you hear?": "🤏 En douce… quel mot entends-tu ?",
  "{p}: “Hey! THIEF!”": "{p} : « Hé ! AU VOLEUR ! »",
  "🚨 A town guard grabs you by the collar!": "🚨 Un garde du village t'attrape par le col !",
  "Off to the jail you go…": "Direction la prison…",
  "🤫 Your fingers slip into their pocket…": "🤫 Tes doigts se glissent dans sa poche…",
  "💰 <b>{n} gold</b>! {p} didn’t notice a thing.": "💰 <b>{n} pièces d'or</b> ! {p} n'a rien remarqué.",
  "{p} {p} ×{n} · {n} gold each": "{p} {p} ×{n} · {n} pièces d'or chacun",
  "Sells one. All {n} are worth {n} gold.": "En vend un. Les {n} valent {n} pièces d'or.",
  "You sold the {p} for 💰 {n} gold.": "Tu as vendu {p} pour 💰 {n} pièces d'or.",
  "💰 Sell treasures · you have 💰 {n} gold": "💰 Vendre des trésors · tu as 💰 {n} pièces d'or",
  "💰 Sell everything ({n} gold)": "💰 Tout vendre ({n} pièces d'or)",
  "Sold! 💰 +{n} gold.": "Vendu ! 💰 +{n} pièces d'or.",
  "💰 Sell treasures": "💰 Vendre des trésors",
});
GT_BOOKS.fr.suffix.push(...[[" · Jail"," · Prison"],[" · 1F"," · É1"],[" · 2F"," · É2"]]);
Object.assign(GT_BOOKS.ja.names, {"Brother Ansel":"アンセル修道士","Sister Imane":"シスター・イマーン","Mother Solenne":"マザー・ソレンヌ","Brother Tobiah":"トビア修道士","Old Hob":"ホブじいさん","Father Edric":"エドリック神父","Mabel":"メイベル","Sister Ama":"シスター・アマ","Jasir":"ジャシール","Brother Kaveh":"カヴェ修道士","Captain Nell":"ネル船長","Mother Liane":"マザー・リアン","Zaid":"ザイド","Brother Rafi":"ラフィ修道士","Pell":"ペル","Sister Moira":"シスター・モイラ","Ingrid":"イングリッド","Father Aksel":"アクセル神父","Ottoline":"オットリン","Mother Iris":"マザー・アイリス","Brannoc":"ブラノック","Brother Cael":"ケイル修道士","Sister Wynne":"シスター・ウィン","Father Lumen":"ルーメン神父","Frostmark Tundra":"フロストマーク凍原","Wandering priest":"旅の神父","Thundercrag Highlands":"サンダークラッグ高地","Inkblight Wastes":"インクブライト荒野","Verdant Wilds":"ヴァーダント原野","Mirefen Marsh":"マイアフェン湿地","Sunscorch Canyon":"サンスコーチ峡谷","Olaf":"オーラフ","Mother Frida":"マザー・フリーダ","Greta":"グレタ","Brother Hale":"ヘイル修道士","Mags":"マグズ","Father Grey":"グレイ神父","Kofi":"コフィ","Sister Ivy":"シスター・アイビー","Pip":"ピップ","Brother Moss":"モス修道士","Dusty":"ダスティ","Mother Sol":"マザー・ソル","Castle Unwritten · Hall of Flames":"書かれざる城・炎の間","Castle Unwritten · Hall of Hours":"書かれざる城・時の間","Castle Unwritten · Hall of Voices":"書かれざる城・声の間","Castle Unwritten":"書かれざる城","Merchant":"商人","Sea trader":"海の商人","Harbor priest":"港の神父","Salty Brin":"しおからブリン","Salty Fros":"しおからフロス","Salty Palm":"しおからパーム","Salty Tide":"しおからタイド","Far Northwest Sea":"北西のはての海","Frozen Sea":"こおった海","Northern Sea":"北の海","Ink Sea":"インクの海","Far Northeast Sea":"北東のはての海","Frostwater Sea":"氷水の海","Blackwater Sea":"黒い水の海","Western Sea":"西の海","Eastern Ocean":"東の大洋","Jungle Sea":"ジャングルの海","Sunset Sea":"夕日の海","Far Southwest Sea":"南西のはての海","Coral Sea":"珊瑚の海","Southern Sea":"南の海","Ember Sea":"残り火の海","Far Southeast Sea":"南東のはての海","Castle Quillhaven":"クイルヘイブン城","Queen Maren":"マレン王妃","Royal guard":"近衛兵","Prince Edwin":"エドウィン王子","Librarian Ottilie":"司書オッティリー","Page boy":"小姓","Cook Barnaby":"コックのバーナビー","Kitchen maid":"台所のメイド","Off-duty guard":"非番の衛兵","Captain Hale":"ヘイル隊長","Princess Rosalind":"ロザリンド王女","Lady’s maid":"侍女","Chancellor Voss":"ヴォス大臣","Lady Abigail":"アビゲイル夫人","Treasury guard":"宝物庫の衛兵","Castle maid":"城のメイド","Gate guard":"門番","Lumen Palace":"ルーメン宮殿","Prince Tariq":"タリク王子","Palace guard":"宮殿の衛兵","Map keeper Idris":"地図番イドリス","Scholar":"学者","Cook Samira":"コックのサミーラ","Captain Zara":"ザラ隊長","Princess Leila":"レイラ王女","Vizier Omar":"オマル宰相","Ambassador Lys":"リス大使","Palace maid":"宮殿のメイド","Jailer":"牢番","Prisoner":"囚人","Old prisoner":"年老いた囚人","Townsperson":"町の人","Sea glass":"シーグラス","Conch shell":"ほら貝","Silver ring":"銀の指輪","Pearl":"真珠","Coral idol":"珊瑚の像","Gold doubloons":"ドブロン金貨","Sunken crown":"しずんだかんむり","Star sapphire":"スターサファイア","Frost Wolf":"霜オオカミ","Snow Owl":"雪フクロウ","Ice Crab":"氷ガニ","Frost Moth":"霜のガ","Ice Golem":"氷ゴーレム","Crag Rat":"岩ネズミ","Thunder Hawk":"雷タカ","Storm Imp":"嵐の小鬼","Iron Beetle":"鉄カブト","Boulder Brute":"大岩ブルート","Ink Ooze":"インクスライム","Blight Wraith":"荒野の亡霊","Rot Bat":"くさりコウモリ","Hollow Knight":"からっぽ騎士","Cursed Grimoire":"のろいの魔導書","Vine Serpent":"つるヘビ","Jungle Toadstool":"ジャングルダケ","Thorn Sprite":"いばら精","Jungle Parrot":"ジャングルオウム","Jade Beetle":"ヒスイカブト","Bog Blob":"沼ブロブ","Rot Cap":"くさりダケ","Swamp Eel":"沼ウナギ","Mud Crab":"どろガニ","Marsh Moth":"湿地のガ","Dust Coyote":"砂ぼこりコヨーテ","Saguaro Brute":"サワロブルート","Canyon Vulture":"峡谷ハゲワシ","Mesa Golem":"台地ゴーレム","Sun Scarab":"太陽スカラベ","The Glacier Wyrm":"氷河の竜","The Storm Roc":"嵐のロック鳥","The Lich Scribe":"リッチの書記","The Vine Hydra":"つるのヒドラ","The Mire Queen":"どろの女王","The Canyon Wyvern":"峡谷のワイバーン","The Silent Herald":"沈黙の伝令","Ink Sentinel":"インクの番兵","Hoarfrost Cavern":"霜の洞くつ","Thunder Mine":"雷の鉱山","Blighted Crypt":"朽ちた地下墓所","Overgrown Temple":"草にうもれた神殿","Drowned Barrow":"しずんだ塚","Echo Canyon Caves":"こだま峡谷の洞くつ","Ruby Key":"ルビーの鍵","Sapphire Key":"サファイアの鍵","Emerald Key":"エメラルドの鍵","Dawn Quill":"夜明けの羽ペン","Dusk Inkwell":"夕暮れのインク壺","Star Seal":"星の印章","Statue of Dawn":"夜明けの像","Statue of Noon":"真昼の像","Statue of Dusk":"夕暮れの像"});
Object.assign(GT_BOOKS.ja.lines, {
  "Through the doors, a throne of black ink. The air goes perfectly still. Not a sound. Not even your own steps.": "扉の向こうに、黒いインクの玉座。空気はぴたりと止まっている。音ひとつない。自分の足音さえ。",
  "A tall figure in a robe of blank pages rises from it. Where his words should be, there is only ink.": "白紙のページのローブを着た背の高い人影が、そこから立ち上がる。言葉があるはずの場所には、インクしかない。",
  "{p}: You found my keys. You solved my riddles. How tiresome.": "{p}：鍵を見つけ、なぞを解いたか。まったく、めんどうなことだ。",
  "{p}: Words. Noisy, messy, endless words. I will unwrite you first.": "{p}：言葉。うるさくて、ちらかった、終わりのない言葉。まずおまえを書き消してやる。",
  "💎 The {p}’s voice bursts out of the Unwriter’s throne, and the shards begin to sing.": "💎 {p}の声がアンライターの玉座からあふれ出し、かけらが歌いはじめた。",
  "At the top of the tower, a knight in black armor stands perfectly still.": "塔のてっぺんで、黒いよろいの騎士がぴくりとも動かずに立っている。",
  "He has no mouth. When he speaks, the words appear in the air like smoke.": "口がない。話すと、言葉がけむりのように空中にあらわれる。",
  "{p}: My master is not here. But his shards are. And I will keep them.": "{p}：わが主はここにはいない。だが、主のかけらはここにある。それはわたしが守る。",
  "The Herald’s armor falls apart, empty. A last smoky word drifts away: “castle”.": "伝令のよろいがくずれ落ちる。中はからっぽだ。最後のけむりの言葉がただよっていく：「城」。",
  "Behind him, the shards of the {p} glow on a stone table.": "そのうしろで、{p}のかけらが石の台の上で光っている。",
  "💎 You found the <b>last {p} Shards</b>! Every shard is together at last, but they are silent.": "💎 <b>最後の{p}のかけら</b>を見つけた！ ついにすべてがそろった。だが、だまったままだ。",
  "{p} has hidden away the {p}’s voice.": "{p0}が{p1}の声をかくしてしまった。",
  "Take the shards home to {p} in {p}, {p}.": "{p2}、かけらを{p1}にいる{p0}のもとへ持ち帰ろう。",
  "{p}: {p}… all the shards. I never dreamed I would see the whole {p} again.": "{p0}：{p1}…すべてのかけらだ。{p2}がそろうのを見られる日が来るとは思わなかった。",
  "But listen: it does not sing. {p} has locked its voice away in <b>Castle Unwritten</b>, in the {p} far to the north-east.": "だが聞いてくれ：歌わないのだ。{p0}はその声を、はるか北東の{p1}にある<b>書かれざる城</b>に閉じこめた。",
  "The castle gate opens only for three keys, hidden long ago at the edges of the world:": "城の門が開くのは三つの鍵だけ。むかし、世界のはしにかくされたものだ：",
  "🪶 the <b>Dawn Quill</b>, high in the {p} in the north,": "🪶 北の{p}の高みにある<b>夜明けの羽ペン</b>、",
  "🫙 the <b>Dusk Inkwell</b>, lost in the {p} in the south,": "🫙 南の{p}で失われた<b>夕暮れのインク壺</b>、",
  "⭐ and the <b>Star Seal</b>, fallen into the {p} in the far south.": "⭐ そして、はるか南の{p}に落ちた<b>星の印章</b>だ。",
  "I have ordered the old roads opened: north and south of Aldermere, north and south of Seravel. Your ship can sail north and south from the Eastern Isles too.": "古い道を開くよう命じた：オルダミアとセラベルの北と南だ。きみの船も、東の島々から北と南へ進めるようになった。",
  "Ask in the taverns. People remember more than they think. Go, and bring back our words!": "酒場でたずねてみなさい。人は自分で思うより多くのことを覚えているものだ。行け、そしてわれらの言葉を取りもどしてくれ！",
  "{p}: All three keys! Castle Unwritten is in the {p}, far to the north-east. End this, hero.": "{p}：三つの鍵がそろった！ 書かれざる城ははるか北東の{p}にある。終わらせてくれ、勇者よ。",
  "✨ Something glints between the rocks… you dig it out.": "✨ 岩のあいだで何かが光った…掘り出した。",
  "🪶 You found the <b>Dawn Quill</b>! A golden quill that writes light. (Key {n} of {n})": "🪶 <b>夜明けの羽ペン</b>を見つけた！ 光を書く金の羽ペンだ。（鍵 {n}／{n}）",
  "✨ Deep in the trees, a little pool of shadow… no, an inkwell, sitting on a mossy stone.": "✨ 木々の奥に、小さな影の水たまり…いや、こけむした石の上のインク壺だ。",
  "🫙 You found the <b>Dusk Inkwell</b>! Its ink is the color of the evening sky. (Key {n} of {n})": "🫙 <b>夕暮れのインク壺</b>を見つけた！ インクは夕方の空の色だ。（鍵 {n}／{n}）",
  "✨ Something in the dust of the gully twinkles like a fallen star.": "✨ 谷のほこりの中で、何かが落ちた星のようにまたたいている。",
  "⭐ You found the <b>Star Seal</b>! A silver seal shaped like a star. (Key {n} of {n})": "⭐ <b>星の印章</b>を見つけた！ 星の形をした銀の印章だ。（鍵 {n}／{n}）",
  "🔑 The quill, the inkwell and the star hum together in your bag.": "🔑 羽ペン、インク壺、星が、ふくろの中でいっしょにひびいている。",
  "Castle Unwritten’s gate will open for you now. It stands in the {p}, in the far north-east.": "これで書かれざる城の門が開く。城ははるか北東の{p}にある。",
  "The cave floor is a frozen lake. Under the ice, two cold eyes open.": "洞くつの床はこおった湖だ。氷の下で、冷たい目がふたつ開いた。",
  "A wyrm of ice smashes up through the floor!": "氷の竜が床をつきやぶって出てきた！",
  "{p} shatters into a thousand glittering pieces.": "{p}はきらめく千のかけらになってくだけた。",
  "Wind howls up the shaft. A giant bird made of storm clouds lands in front of you.": "たて穴を風がほえる。嵐の雲でできた巨大な鳥が目の前におりてきた。",
  "{p}: SKREEEEE!": "{p}：キシャアアアア！",
  "{p} dissolves into a harmless spring rain.": "{p}はおだやかな春の雨になって消えた。",
  "A skeleton in a scholar’s robe looks up from a book of black pages.": "学者のローブを着たがいこつが、黒いページの本から顔を上げた。",
  "{p}: Ah, visitors. Let me write you… an ending.": "{p}：おや、お客さまか。書いてあげよう…おまえたちの結末を。",
  "{p}’s book slams shut, and he crumbles to dust with it.": "{p}の本がバタンと閉じ、彼もいっしょにちりになった。",
  "The temple floor cracks. Vines as thick as trees rise up, each with a snapping head.": "神殿の床がひび割れた。木のように太いつるが立ち上がり、それぞれにかみつく頭がある。",
  "{p} hisses from three mouths at once!": "{p}は三つの口でいっせいにシューッと鳴いた！",
  "{p} withers and sinks back into the ground.": "{p}はしおれて、地面にしずんでいった。",
  "The water in the barrow bubbles. A huge shape of mud and weeds rises, wearing a crown of reeds.": "塚の水があわ立つ。あしのかんむりをかぶった、どろと水草の巨大な姿が立ち上がる。",
  "{p}: You are tracking mud into my palace!": "{p}：わたくしの宮殿をどろだらけにしないで！",
  "{p} slumps back into a harmless puddle. Her crown floats away.": "{p}はただの水たまりにくずれた。かんむりがぷかぷか流れていく。",
  "Hot wind fills the cave. A red wyvern drops from the ceiling, wings spread wide.": "熱い風が洞くつをみたす。赤いワイバーンがつばさを広げて天井から落ちてきた。",
  "{p} roars, and the whole canyon roars with it!": "{p}がほえると、峡谷じゅうがいっしょにほえた！",
  "{p} flees out of a crack in the rock, never to return.": "{p}は岩のさけ目からにげ去り、二度ともどらなかった。",
  "💰 {p} guarded a pile of treasure!": "💰 {p}は宝の山を守っていた！",
  "💰 {p}’s nest is full of shiny things!": "💰 {p}の巣は光る物でいっぱいだ！",
  "💰 {p}’s hoard is yours!": "💰 {p}のお宝はきみのものだ！",
  "💰 Treasure hidden among the roots!": "💰 根っこのあいだに宝がかくれていた！",
  "💰 {p}’s treasure, a little muddy.": "💰 {p}の宝。ちょっとどろだらけ。",
  "💰 The wyvern’s hoard glitters in the dark!": "💰 ワイバーンのお宝が暗やみで光っている！",
  "The three keys rise out of your bag and fit into the sockets.": "三つの鍵がふくろから浮かび上がり、くぼみにはまった。",
  "With a sound like a book opening, Castle Unwritten’s gate swings wide.": "本が開くような音とともに、書かれざる城の門が大きく開いた。",
  "You pull the {p} lever. Its flame goes out.": "{p}のレバーを引いた。火が消えた。",
  "🔥 Sun, star… and the moon asleep. The iron gate grinds upward!": "🔥 太陽、星…そしてねむる月。鉄の格子がきしみながら上がっていく！",
  "✨ The plate glows.": "✨ 床の板が光った。",
  "The plates sink back into the floor with a groan.": "床の板がうなりながらもとにしずんだ。",
  "Read the poem again: in what order does the night pass?": "もう一度詩を読もう：夜はどんな順番で過ぎていく？",
  "🔥 All four plates blaze with light. The iron gate grinds upward!": "🔥 四枚の床の板がすべて光りかがやいた。鉄の格子がきしみながら上がっていく！",
  "🗿 {p}: “Answer my word, traveler.”": "🗿 {p}：「わが言葉に答えよ、旅人。」",
  "🗿 {p}: “True words.” Its eyes glow gold.": "🗿 {p}：「まことの言葉だ。」目が金色に光る。",
  "🗿 {p}: “Not true. Come back when you know.”": "🗿 {p}：「まことではない。わかったら、また来るがいい。」",
  "🗿 All three statues glow. The great doors to the throne room swing open!": "🗿 三体の像がすべて光った。玉座の間の大きな扉が開く！",
  "Welcome to {p}. The King awaits brave souls.": "{p}へようこそ。王様は勇気ある者を待っておられる。",
  "{p}’s last guards block the stairs!": "{p}の最後の護衛が階段をふさいでいる！",
  "Keep warm! The {p} Wolves hunt in packs out on the tundra.": "あたたかくしてね！ {p}のオオカミが凍原で群れをなして狩りをしているよ。",
  "East of here the land turns to rock and thunder: the {p}.": "ここから東は、岩と雷の土地：{p}だ。",
  "I built a snow knight yesterday. It has a sword made of an icicle!": "きのう雪の騎士を作ったんだ。つららの剣を持ってるよ！",
  "Thunder Hawks steal our hats. Every. Single. Day.": "雷のタカがぼくらのぼうしをぬすんでいく。毎日。毎日。",
  "Further east the land goes black. Nothing grows in the {p}.": "もっと東は土地が黒くなる。{p}では何も育たない。",
  "The mine’s gold paid for this town. Now monsters dig there instead.": "鉱山の金がこの町を作った。今はモンスターがそこを掘っているよ。",
  "We are the last town before the castle. Buy {p}: the wraiths out there love curses.": "ここは城の前の最後の町だ。{p}を買っていけ。外の亡霊はのろいが大好きなんだ。",
  "The Blighted Crypt is north-west of here. A Lich Scribe writes death verses down there.": "朽ちた地下墓所はここから北西。リッチの書記が下で死の詩を書いている。",
  "Mum says not to look at the castle at night. I looked. It looked back.": "夜に城を見ちゃだめってママが言うの。見ちゃった。むこうも見かえしてきた。",
  "Vine Serpents bite. Carry Antidotes, always.": "つるのヘビはかみつく。いつでもどくけしを持っておきな。",
  "North is Aldermere. East is the {p}. Mind your boots.": "北はオルダミア。東は{p}。足もとに気をつけてね。",
  "A parrot taught me a rude word. I won’t say it.": "オウムに悪い言葉を教わったんだ。言わないけど。",
  "Rot Caps puff poison. Hold your breath. Or just bring Antidotes.": "くさりダケは毒を吹く。息を止めな。それか、どくけしを持っていきな。",
  "The road north goes back up to Seravel, through the canyon road.": "北の道は峡谷の道を通ってセラベルへもどる。",
  "I caught a frog the size of my head! Then it caught me.": "頭くらい大きいカエルをつかまえたよ！ そしたらカエルにつかまった。",
  "The sea north of here leads back to the Eastern Isles, if you have a boat.": "ここから北の海は、船があれば東の島々にもどれるよ。",
  "Sun Scarabs flash so bright you can’t see. Squint!": "太陽のスカラベはまぶしくて何も見えない。目を細めて！",
  "Yell in the canyon and it yells back. I yelled my name forty times.": "峡谷でさけぶと、さけび返してくるんだ。自分の名前を四十回さけんだよ。",
  "The way ahead is guarded!": "この先は見張られている！",
  "The Hoarfrost Cavern is north-east of town. Something huge sleeps in the ice down there.": "霜の洞くつは町の北東にある。下の氷の中で、何か巨大なものがねむっている。",
  "The old road south goes back to Aldermere. The King opened it for you, they say.": "南の古い道はオルダミアへもどる。王様がきみのために開いたんだってさ。",
  "Pray, rest, and be brave. {p} fears words spoken with courage.": "いのり、休み、勇気を持て。{p}は勇気をもって語られる言葉をおそれている。",
  "The Dawn Quill? A shepherd swore she saw a golden glint on the peak above the old mine, in the north-west.": "夜明けの羽ペン？ 北西の古い鉱山の上の峰で、金色の光を見たって羊かいが言ってたよ。",
  "The Thunder Mine runs deep. A Storm Roc nests at the bottom.": "雷の鉱山はとても深い。いちばん下に嵐のロック鳥が巣を作っている。",
  "Castle Unwritten is east of town. Its gate has three sockets: a quill, an inkwell and a star.": "書かれざる城は町の東だ。門には三つのくぼみがある：羽ペン、インク壺、星。",
  "Inside the castle, the old guards say, the doors only open for the clever. Levers, plates and talking statues.": "城の中の扉は、かしこい者にしか開かないと、古い衛兵たちは言う。レバー、床の板、それにしゃべる像だ。",
  "The Dusk Inkwell? Old Ma {p} talks about a grove nobody can find, deep in the trees in the south-east.": "夕暮れのインク壺？ マ・{p}ばあさんが、南東の森の奥にだれも見つけられない木立があるって話しているよ。",
  "The Overgrown Temple is north-east. A Vine Hydra grew out of the floor in there!": "草にうもれた神殿は北東だ。中の床からつるのヒドラが生えてきたんだって！",
  "The Drowned Barrow is south-west of town, past the reeds. {p} rules it.": "しずんだ塚は町の南西、あしの原の先。{p}が支配している。",
  "The canyon east of here is dry as bone. Opposite of here, really.": "ここから東の峡谷は骨みたいにからからだ。ここと正反対だね。",
  "The Star Seal? There’s a gully in the far west, past the red cliffs, where the stars fall at night.": "星の印章？ はるか西、赤いがけの先に、夜に星が落ちてくる谷があるよ。",
  "The Echo Canyon Caves are south-east. A Canyon Wyvern roosts at the bottom.": "こだま峡谷の洞くつは南東。いちばん下に峡谷のワイバーンがいる。",
  "🪨 Words are carved into the stone:": "🪨 石に言葉がきざまれている：",
  "“Wake the Sun and the Star, but let the Moon sleep.”": "「太陽と星を起こせ。だが月はねむらせておけ。」",
  "“Beware: every lever stirs the one beside it.”": "「気をつけよ：レバーはどれも、となりのレバーを動かす。」",
  "Two Ink Sentinels step out of the shadows!": "インクの番兵が二体、かげから出てきた！",
  "🪨 A poem is carved into the stone:": "🪨 石に詩がきざまれている：",
  "“First the quill writes the dawn, then the sun climbs high,”": "「まず羽ペンが夜明けを書き、つぎに太陽が高くのぼり、」",
  "“the moon follows after, and a star closes the sky.”": "「月があとにつづき、星が空を閉じる。」",
  "Four plates are set into the floor: 🪶 ☀️ 🌙 ⭐": "床に四枚の板がある：🪶 ☀️ 🌙 ⭐",
  "The Statue of Dawn": "夜明けの像",
  "The Statue of Noon": "真昼の像",
  "The Statue of Dusk": "夕暮れの像",
  "🪨 “Speak true words to the three statues, and the last door will open.”": "🪨 「三体の像にまことの言葉を語れ。さすれば最後の扉が開く。」",
  "{p}: Rare goods from across the sea! Take a look.": "{p}：海の向こうのめずらしい品だよ！ 見ていって。",
  "{p}: Blades and bows from faraway smithies!": "{p}：遠くのかじ屋の剣と弓だよ！",
  "Welcome to {p}, the west harbor of Aldermere! Ships come and go all day.": "オルダミアの西の港、{p}へようこそ！ 一日じゅう船が出入りしているよ。",
  "Sail north along the coast and you reach the {p}. South takes you to the jungle.": "海岸ぞいに北へ進めば{p}に着く。南へ行けばジャングルだ。",
  "There’s a shrine on a little island just south of here. Sailors pray there before a long trip.": "すぐ南の小島にほこらがある。船乗りは長い旅の前にそこでいのるんだ。",
  "{p} never freezes. The sea keeps moving, so the ice can’t catch it.": "{p}はこおらない。海がいつも動いているから、氷が追いつけないんだ。",
  "East along the north coast is the Thundercrag shore, and past that, the black Inkblight sea.": "北の海岸を東へ行くとサンダークラッグの浜、その先は黒いインクブライトの海だ。",
  "An island shrine sits just off the coast, north of here. Ice all around it, but warm inside.": "ここから北、海岸のすぐ沖の島にほこらがある。まわりは氷だらけだけど、中はあたたかいよ。",
  "{p}! Best fish on the whole continent. Don’t tell the Marsh folk I said that.": "{p}！ 大陸でいちばんの魚だよ。湿地の連中には、わたしが言ったってないしょね。",
  "You can sail up the river from here, right into the heart of the jungle.": "ここから川をさかのぼって、ジャングルのまん中まで行けるよ。",
  "East along the coast is {p}, then the red canyon. The whole south shore is one long sea road.": "海岸を東へ行くと{p}、その先は赤い峡谷。南の海岸はぜんぶ一本の長い海の道だよ。",
  "{p} sits where the marsh meets the sea. Mind the eels at low tide.": "{p}は湿地と海が出会う場所にある。干潮のときはウナギに気をつけて。",
  "The sea lanes go all the way round the continent now that the King opened them.": "王様が開いてくれたから、海の道は大陸をぐるりと一周しているよ。",
  "Old story: there’s a shrine out on the water, east of here, that heals even the fallen.": "むかし話：ここから東の海の上に、たおれた者まで治すほこらがあるんだって。",
  "Every coast of the continent is linked by sea now. Sail all the way round if you like!": "大陸の海岸はぜんぶ海でつながったよ。よければぐるっと一周してごらん！",
  "Island shrines heal the whole crew. Steer close and pray from the deck.": "島のほこらは船の仲間みんなを治してくれる。近くまで行って甲板からいのってね。",
  "I pray here before every voyage. The sea is kinder to the faithful.": "航海の前にはいつもここでいのるんです。海は信じる者にやさしいから。",
  "{p}: Welcome to our home, young hero. Do look around. The library is my favourite room.": "{p}：わが家へようこそ、若い勇者さん。ゆっくり見ていってね。図書室がわたしのお気に入りよ。",
  "{p}: The cook makes the best honey bread in the kingdom. Tell him I sent you.": "{p}：コックの作るはちみつパンは王国一よ。わたしに言われて来たと伝えてね。",
  "{p}: Stand tall before the King!": "{p}：王様の前では背すじをのばせ！",
  "{p}: Nobody gets near the thrones without our say-so.": "{p}：われわれの許しなく、玉座に近づける者はいない。",
  "{p}: One day I’ll go on an adventure too! Father says I must learn my words first.": "{p}：いつかぼくも冒険に出るんだ！ 父上は、まず言葉をおぼえなさいって言うけど。",
  "{p}: Did you know there are chests in three colors? Ruby, sapphire and emerald. Each needs its own key.": "{p}：宝箱には三つの色があるって知ってた？ ルビー、サファイア、エメラルド。それぞれに専用の鍵がいるんだ。",
  "{p}: Shh! This is the royal library. Every book here was written with the old {p}.": "{p}：しーっ！ ここは王家の図書室です。ここの本はすべて、古い{p}で書かれたのですよ。",
  "{p}: Read a little every day and the words will stay with you.": "{p}：毎日少しずつ読めば、言葉はあなたのそばに残ります。",
  "{p}: I’m supposed to be dusting the shelves… but this book about sea monsters is really good.": "{p}：本当は棚のほこりをはらう係なんだけど…この海の怪物の本がすごくおもしろくて。",
  "{p}: Mind the hot stove! Honey bread for the King, stew for the guards.": "{p}：熱いかまどに気をつけな！ 王様にははちみつパン、衛兵にはシチューだ。",
  "{p}: Hungry? Inns are the place for a hot meal and a warm bed.": "{p}：おなかすいた？ あたたかい食事とベッドなら宿屋だよ。",
  "{p}: Twelve loaves, six pies and a cake for the Prince. And the day has only started!": "{p}：パン十二個、パイ六つ、王子さまのケーキがひとつ。一日はまだはじまったばかり！",
  "{p}: Night shift tonight. I’m resting my feet while I can.": "{p}：今夜は夜勤だ。今のうちに足を休めておくよ。",
  "{p}: My guards keep the towns safe. If you see a pickpocket, call for us!": "{p}：わたしの衛兵が町を守っている。すりを見かけたら呼んでくれ！",
  "{p}: Every town has a jail now. Thieves spend a night behind bars, or pay a fine.": "{p}：今はどの町にも牢屋がある。泥棒はひと晩鉄格子の向こうで過ごすか、罰金をはらうのだ。",
  "{p}: Father keeps the Ruby Key in the treasury, downstairs on this side.": "{p}：父上はルビーの鍵を宝物庫にしまっているわ。こちら側の下の階よ。",
  "{p}: {p} of Seravel keeps the Sapphire Key. And the Emerald Key? Lost at sea, somewhere far to the south-east.": "{p0}：セラベルの{p1}がサファイアの鍵を持っているわ。エメラルドの鍵は？ 海で失われたの。はるか南東のどこかで。",
  "{p}: The Princess’s room must be spotless. She notices every speck of dust!": "{p}：王女さまのお部屋はぴかぴかでなくては。ほこりひとつでも気づかれるのよ！",
  "{p}: The royal dinner is at sundown. Forty guests, sixty candles.": "{p}：王家の夕食は日暮れどき。客人四十人、ろうそく六十本。",
  "{p}: Taxes, letters, maps… a chancellor’s work is never done.": "{p}：税金、手紙、地図…大臣の仕事に終わりはない。",
  "{p}: I came all the way from {p} for the feast. Isn’t the hall lovely?": "{p}：宴のために、はるばる{p}から来ましたの。すてきな広間でしょう？",
  "{p}: The King says you may open the treasury chests. The Ruby Key is in the locked one.": "{p}：王様が宝物庫の宝箱を開けてよいとおっしゃった。ルビーの鍵は錠のかかった箱の中だ。",
  "{p}: Spell its word to open the lock. Then the key opens every ruby-red chest you find.": "{p}：言葉を書いて錠を開けろ。そうすれば、その鍵で見つけたルビー色の宝箱がぜんぶ開く。",
  "{p}: Good day! The great hall gets so dusty with all these visitors.": "{p}：こんにちは！ お客さんが多いと大広間はほこりだらけになるのよ。",
  "{p}: Welcome to {p}. The King is at the far end of the hall.": "{p}：{p}へようこそ。王様は広間のいちばん奥におられる。",
  "{p}: The town is just outside. Enjoy your visit!": "{p}：町はすぐ外だ。楽しんでいってくれ！",
  "{p}: My mother rules Seravel from this throne. I’m learning to sail, so I can visit every coast!": "{p}：母上はこの玉座からセラベルをおさめている。ぼくはどの海岸にも行けるように、船の練習中なんだ！",
  "{p}: The Sapphire Key? It’s in our treasury, of course. Ask the guard there.": "{p}：サファイアの鍵？ もちろん、うちの宝物庫にあるよ。そこの衛兵に聞いてごらん。",
  "{p}: Bow to Her Majesty, {p}!": "{p}：女王陛下、{p}さまに礼を！",
  "{p}: The sun never sets on Seravel. Well… it does. But slowly.": "{p}：セラベルに日は沈まない。まあ…沈むけどね。ゆっくり。",
  "{p}: These shelves hold maps of every coast and island. The seas link all the way round now!": "{p}：この棚には、すべての海岸と島の地図があります。今では海がぐるりとつながっているのです！",
  "{p}: Old charts say the Emerald Key sank with a ship near an island in the south-east.": "{p}：古い海図によれば、エメラルドの鍵は南東の島の近くで船とともにしずんだそうです。",
  "{p}: I am copying a map of the Sunken Archive. One wrong line and someone gets lost!": "{p}：沈んだ書庫の地図を写しているの。線を一本まちがえたら、だれかが迷子になっちゃう！",
  "{p}: Spiced rice, date cakes and mint tea. Palace food is the best in the desert!": "{p}：スパイスのごはん、ナツメヤシのケーキ、ミントティー。宮殿の料理は砂漠いちばんよ！",
  "{p}: Try not to steal from the townsfolk. The jail food is terrible, I hear.": "{p}：町の人から物をぬすんじゃだめよ。牢屋のごはんはひどいらしいわ。",
  "{p}: Fresh oranges from the oasis! The Queen loves them.": "{p}：オアシスのとれたてオレンジ！ 女王さまの大好物よ。",
  "{p}: Sand in my boots again. Sand everywhere!": "{p}：またブーツに砂が。どこもかしこも砂だらけだ！",
  "{p}: My guards watch the market. Pickpockets end up in the town jail.": "{p}：わたしの衛兵が市場を見張っている。すりは町の牢屋行きだ。",
  "{p}: Pay the fine, or work it off with honest words. Your choice.": "{p}：罰金をはらうか、正直な言葉ではたらいて返すか。好きなほうをえらべ。",
  "{p}: A ruby chest, a sapphire chest, an emerald chest… a key for each color. Once you have a key, it’s yours for good.": "{p}：ルビーの宝箱、サファイアの宝箱、エメラルドの宝箱…色ごとに鍵がひとつ。一度手に入れた鍵は、ずっとあなたのものよ。",
  "{p}: I saw a blue sapphire chest in the desert once. Maybe you’ll find it!": "{p}：砂漠で青いサファイアの宝箱を見たことがあるの。あなたなら見つけられるかも！",
  "{p}: The Princess wants her blue silk ready for the feast.": "{p}：王女さまは宴のために青い絹を用意してほしいそうよ。",
  "{p}: The dining hall is ready for the ambassadors from Aldermere.": "{p}：食堂はオルダミアの使節をむかえる準備ができている。",
  "{p}: Every ship that sails the Royal dock brings news from across the sea.": "{p}：王家の桟橋から出る船は、どれも海の向こうの知らせを運んでくる。",
  "{p}: I bring greetings from {p}. What a beautiful palace!": "{p}：{p}からのごあいさつをお持ちしました。なんて美しい宮殿でしょう！",
  "{p}: The Queen allows you into the treasury. The Sapphire Key is in the word-locked chest.": "{p}：女王さまのお許しで、宝物庫に入ってよい。サファイアの鍵はことばの錠の宝箱の中だ。",
  "{p}: Spell its word, and every sapphire-blue chest in the world will open for you.": "{p}：言葉を書け。そうすれば世界じゅうのサファイア色の宝箱がきみのために開く。",
  "{p}: Mind the carpet, it’s freshly brushed!": "{p}：じゅうたんに気をつけて、ブラシをかけたばかりなの！",
  "{p}: Welcome to {p}. Her Majesty is at the end of the hall.": "{p}：{p}へようこそ。陛下は広間のいちばん奥におられる。",
  "{p}: {p} is right outside. Ships leave from the Royal dock.": "{p0}：{p1}はすぐ外だ。船は王家の桟橋から出ている。",
  "{p}: I only borrowed a loaf of bread! Honest!": "{p}：パンをひとつ借りただけなんだ！ 本当だよ！",
  "{p}: Forty years I picked pockets. Then I picked the Captain’s. Big mistake.": "{p}：四十年、すりをやってきた。そして隊長のさいふをすった。大失敗さ。",
  "{p}: Keep your hands in your own pockets and you’ll never see the inside of a cell.": "{p}：手を自分のポケットに入れておけば、牢屋の中を見ることはない。",
  "The roads north and south of the old kingdoms are open again. Strange lands out there!": "古い王国の北と南の道がまた開いたよ。外には不思議な土地があるんだって！",
  "Some treasures are hidden in plain sight. Walk where nobody walks.": "宝の中には、目の前にかくれているものもある。だれも歩かない場所を歩いてごらん。",
  "The whole continent is ringed by sea. With a ship you can reach every coast.": "大陸はぐるりと海にかこまれている。船があれば、どの海岸にも行けるよ。",
  "Island shrines! Sail up close and pray from your boat.": "島のほこら！ 船で近づいて、船の上からいのってね。",
  "Watch your purse in the market! There are pickpockets about.": "市場ではさいふに気をつけて！ すりがいるよ。",
  "Every town has a jail now. Thieves get a night behind bars.": "今はどの町にも牢屋がある。泥棒はひと晩、鉄格子の中だ。",
  "Have you seen the colored chests? Ruby, sapphire, emerald… each wants its own key.": "色つきの宝箱を見た？ ルビー、サファイア、エメラルド…それぞれに専用の鍵がいるんだ。",
  "A smooth, frosted pebble of glass. Worth {n} gold at any shop.": "なめらかで、くもったガラスの小石。どの店でも{n}ゴールドになる。",
  "Hold it to your ear and hear the sea. Worth {n} gold.": "耳にあてると海の音が聞こえる。{n}ゴールドになる。",
  "A sailor’s ring, a little tarnished. Worth {n} gold.": "船乗りの指輪。少しくすんでいる。{n}ゴールドになる。",
  "A perfect round pearl. Worth {n} gold.": "まんまるの真珠。{n}ゴールドになる。",
  "A tiny statue carved from red coral. Worth {n} gold.": "赤い珊瑚をほった小さな像。{n}ゴールドになる。",
  "A pouch of old pirate coins. Worth {n} gold.": "古い海賊の金貨の入ったふくろ。{n}ゴールドになる。",
  "A crown from a kingdom lost to the sea. Worth {n} gold.": "海に消えた王国のかんむり。{n}ゴールドになる。",
  "A deep blue gem with a star inside. Worth {n} gold.": "中に星がある深い青の宝石。{n}ゴールドになる。",
  "Snow and fallen rock block the way.": "雪と落ちた岩が道をふさいでいる。",
  "{p} may know how to open the old roads north and south.": "{p}なら、北と南の古い道の開け方を知っているかもしれない。",
  "Thick black fog hangs over the sea to the north.": "北の海に、黒く濃い霧がたちこめている。",
  "{p} may know what lies beyond it.": "{p}なら、その先に何があるか知っているかもしれない。",
  "A wall of storms blocks the southern sea.": "嵐の壁が南の海をふさいでいる。",
  "Black gates as tall as trees. Three empty sockets glow faintly in the stone:": "木のように高い黒い門。石の中で、三つのからっぽのくぼみがかすかに光っている：",
  "a quill, an inkwell and a star. Without all three keys, the castle will not open.": "羽ペン、インク壺、そして星。三つの鍵がそろわないと、城は開かない。",
  "Storms block the open sea.": "嵐が外海をふさいでいる。",
  "{p} may know when the old sea lanes open.": "{p}なら、古い海の道がいつ開くか知っているかもしれない。",
  "You found something!": "何かを見つけた！",
  "🔑 You got the <b>{p}</b>! 🔴": "🔑 <b>{p}</b>を手に入れた！ 🔴",
  "🔑 You got the <b>{p}</b>! 🔵": "🔑 <b>{p}</b>を手に入れた！ 🔵",
  "🔑 You got the <b>{p}</b>! 🟢": "🔑 <b>{p}</b>を手に入れた！ 🟢",
  "It opens every ruby chest in the world, and it stays with you for good.": "世界じゅうのルビーの宝箱を開けられる。そして、ずっときみのものだ。",
  "It opens every sapphire chest in the world, and it stays with you for good.": "世界じゅうのサファイアの宝箱を開けられる。そして、ずっときみのものだ。",
  "It opens every emerald chest in the world, and it stays with you for good.": "世界じゅうのエメラルドの宝箱を開けられる。そして、ずっときみのものだ。",
  "🔴 A ruby chest! Its keyhole is shaped like a ruby.": "🔴 ルビーの宝箱だ！ かぎ穴がルビーの形をしている。",
  "🔵 A sapphire chest! Its keyhole is shaped like a sapphire.": "🔵 サファイアの宝箱だ！ かぎ穴がサファイアの形をしている。",
  "🟢 A emerald chest! Its keyhole is shaped like a emerald.": "🟢 エメラルドの宝箱だ！ かぎ穴がエメラルドの形をしている。",
  "It only opens with the <b>{p}</b>.": "<b>{p}</b>でしか開かない。",
  "The {p} is kept in the treasury of {p}.": "{p0}は{p1}の宝物庫にある。",
  "The {p} is kept in the treasury of {p}, in {p}.": "{p0}は{p2}にある{p1}の宝物庫にある。",
  "Old charts say the {p} lies on a far island in the south-east sea.": "古い海図によれば、{p}は南東の海のはるかな島にあるらしい。",
  "🔑 The {p} turns with a click… 🔴": "🔑 {p}がカチッと回った… 🔴",
  "🔑 The {p} turns with a click… 🔵": "🔑 {p}がカチッと回った… 🔵",
  "🔑 The {p} turns with a click… 🟢": "🔑 {p}がカチッと回った… 🟢",
  "🚨 A guard makes you pay {n} gold back. Behave yourself!": "🚨 衛兵に{n}ゴールドを返させられた。おとなしくしていろ！",
  "🔒 Clang! The cell door slams shut behind you.": "🔒 ガシャン！ 牢屋の扉がうしろで閉まった。",
  "Talk to the {p} through the bars to get out.": "外に出るには、鉄格子ごしに{p}と話そう。",
  "You pay {n} gold.": "{n}ゴールドをはらった。",
  "🔓 Clank! The cell door swings open.": "🔓 ガチャン！ 牢屋の扉が開いた。",
  "{p}: Off you go. And stay out of other folks’ pockets!": "{p}：行っていいぞ。もう人のポケットに手を入れるなよ！",
  "{p}: Visiting? Keep your hands in your own pockets and you’ll never stay here.": "{p}：面会か？ 手を自分のポケットに入れておけば、ここに泊まることはないさ。",
  "👮 {p}: “Caught with your hand in a pocket, eh?” · 💰 {n}": "👮 {p}：「ポケットに手を入れたところをつかまったか？」・💰 {n}",
  "💰 Pay the fine ({n} gold)": "💰 罰金をはらう（{n}ゴールド）",
  "🧽 Scrub the floors (answer {n} words right)": "🧽 床をみがく（{n}語正しく答える）",
  "Honest work, honest words.": "正直な仕事、正直な言葉。",
  "⏳ Wait": "⏳ 待つ",
  "You sit on the cold stone floor. Nobody comes to let you out.": "冷たい石の床にすわる。だれも出しに来てくれない。",
  "✨ The floors are sparkling!": "✨ 床がぴかぴかになった！",
  "{p}: Not bad. Not bad at all.": "{p}：悪くない。ぜんぜん悪くない。",
  "🧽 Scrubbing the floor… {n}/{n}": "🧽 床をみがいている… {n}/{n}",
  "{p}: Missed a spot! Keep going.": "{p}：みがき残しがあるぞ！ つづけろ。",
  "💬 Talk": "💬 話す",
  "🤏 Pick their pocket": "🤏 ポケットをする",
  "They’re watching you now.": "今は見張られている。",
  "Their pockets are empty now.": "ポケットはもうからっぽだ。",
  "A guard is watching! Move away first.": "衛兵が見ている！ まずはなれよう。",
  "Listen for the word and pick it. Wrong means jail!": "言葉を聞いてえらぼう。まちがえたら牢屋行き！",
  "🤏 Sneaky… which word do you hear?": "🤏 こっそり…何の言葉が聞こえる？",
  "{p}: “Hey! THIEF!”": "{p}：「あっ！ どろぼう！」",
  "🚨 A town guard grabs you by the collar!": "🚨 町の衛兵にえりくびをつかまれた！",
  "Off to the jail you go…": "牢屋へ行くぞ…",
  "🤫 Your fingers slip into their pocket…": "🤫 指がそっとポケットにすべりこむ…",
  "💰 <b>{n} gold</b>! {p} didn’t notice a thing.": "💰 <b>{n}ゴールド</b>！ {p}はまったく気づかなかった。",
  "{p} {p} ×{n} · {n} gold each": "{p} {p} ×{n}・1こ{n}ゴールド",
  "Sells one. All {n} are worth {n} gold.": "ひとつ売る。{n}こぜんぶで{n}ゴールドになる。",
  "You sold the {p} for 💰 {n} gold.": "{p}を売って💰 {n}ゴールドになった。",
  "💰 Sell treasures · you have 💰 {n} gold": "💰 宝を売る・所持金 💰 {n}ゴールド",
  "💰 Sell everything ({n} gold)": "💰 ぜんぶ売る（{n}ゴールド）",
  "Sold! 💰 +{n} gold.": "売れた！ 💰 +{n}ゴールド。",
  "💰 Sell treasures": "💰 宝を売る",
});
